Package: softglowos-installer
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Kevin Schmidt <https://github.com/kevinschmidt777/softglowos>
Homepage: https://softglowos.com
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: softglowos-base, softglowos-hub, softglowos-vendor-apps, calamares, casper, sudo,
 pciutils, ubuntu-drivers-common, grub-efi-amd64-signed, shim-signed, efibootmgr, rsync,
 bluez, python3-gi, gir1.2-adw-1, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-gudev-1.0
Description: SoftglowOS installer for the live system
 Calamares with SoftglowOS's branding, opened on its own in the live session
 of the ISO. It installs Ubuntu's signed NVIDIA driver from the ISO where
 there's an NVIDIA card. Only part of the live system: while it's installed,
 the setup assistant, crash reports and the Chrome/Discord timer are off;
 Calamares removes it from the installed system, which turns them back on.
 Without a mouse or keyboard it first pairs Bluetooth ones.
